In the discussion, James expressed interest in researching geoengineering, specifically Solar Radiation Management (SRM), and inquired whether it aligns with NASA's Mission Directorates. I highlighted that SRM isn’t explicitly covered in the provided categories but identified two relevant directorates. Firstly, the Science Mission Directorate (SMD) could support research on SRM's impacts on Earth's climate system under the Earth Science area. Secondly, the Space Technology Mission Directorate (STMD) might be a fit if the research involves novel technologies related to SRM, such as deployment mechanisms or monitoring tools. I encouraged James to frame his proposal around Earth system science or technological innovation to enhance compatibility with NASA's missions and suggested exploring potential collaborations with other agencies focused on climate engineering.
